  "answer_text": "It looks like you may be referring to **Iuka, Mississippi** (sometimes misspelled as \"Luka\"). Here's an overview:\n\n## Iuka, Mississippi\n\n**Iuka** (/a\u026a\u02c8ju\u02d0k\u0259/) is a city and the county seat of **Tishomingo County, Mississippi**, United States. Its population was **3,139** at the 2020 census.\n\n### Geography\nIuka is located in **northeast Mississippi**. **Woodall Mountain**, the highest point in Mississippi, is located just south of Iuka.\n\n### History\nIuka is built on the site of a **Chickasaw village**, and the name \"Iuka\" comes from the name of one of the chiefs of that village. It was founded by David Hubbard, a wagon train scout, and Euro-American settlers arrived with the **Memphis and Charleston Railroad in 1857**.\n\nBefore the American Civil War, the town boasted an all-female college, a boys' military academy, and a fine hotel. The Civil War brought widespread devastation when a major engagement occurred on **September 19, 1862** \u2014 the **Battle of Iuka** \u2014 resulting in 1,200 to 1,500 killed or wounded.\n\n### Natural Attractions\nSix artesian springs flow to the surface in Iuka at **Iuka Springs Park**, though currently only three springs are still flowing. They are located in a public park and are accessible.\n\n### Demographics\nAs of the 2020 census, Iuka had a population of 3,139, with a median age of 43.5 years. About 21.9% of residents were under 18, and 24.7% were 65 or older.\n\nWould you like to know more about Iuka, Mississippi, or were you referring to something else by \"Luka Mississippi\"?",
